let BEATS=[
 {word:'BEGINNING',scramble:'GNINNIGEB',clue:'What does Genesis place before the six creative periods, without giving it a date?',period:'BEFORE THE SIX CREATIVE PERIODS',title:'A beginning without a date',fact:'Genesis 1:1 describes the heavens and earth already created before the six periods begin. The Bible does not give the age of the universe.',scene:'ocean',pos:'center 49%',reference:'Genesis 1:1–2'},
 {word:'DIFFUSED',scramble:'DESUFFID',clue:'Day became distinguishable before the sun was clearly visible. What kind of light apparently reached the surface?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD ONE',title:'A change in the darkness',fact:'The first period describes light reaching earth. JW.org explains that this could have been diffused light through the atmosphere—not the first creation of the sun.',scene:'light',pos:'center 59%',reference:'Genesis 1:3–5'},
 {word:'EXPANSE',scramble:'ESNAPXE',clue:'Which feature separated the waters below from the waters above in the second period?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD TWO',title:'Space between the waters',fact:'The expanse separated waters below from waters above. The Bible calls that expanse Heaven (Genesis 1:6–8).',scene:'sky',pos:'center 45%',reference:'Genesis 1:6–8'},
 {word:'HABITABLE',scramble:'ELBATIBAH',clue:'First light, then an expanse, then dry ground: what was the earth gradually becoming for future life?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD THREE',title:'A planet taking shape',fact:'The emergence of dry ground was part of the earth becoming habitable. Genesis describes a sequence of preparation rather than a planet instantly filled with life.',scene:'genesis_land',pos:'center 50%',reference:'Genesis 1:9–10'},
 {word:'KINDS',scramble:'SDNIK',clue:'Genesis repeatedly says vegetation would reproduce according to its what?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD THREE',title:'Life that keeps growing',fact:'Seed-bearing plants and fruit trees reproduce according to their kinds. The account emphasizes continuing life, not just a single garden appearing.',scene:'genesis_plants',pos:'center 52%',reference:'Genesis 1:11–13'},
 {word:'SEASONS',scramble:'SNOSAES',clue:'The visible heavenly luminaries served as signs for days, years, and what other recurring divisions?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD FOUR',title:'Time written in the sky',fact:'Genesis describes the luminaries marking seasons, days, and years. They became discernible from the earth during the fourth period; this need not mean they were first created then.',scene:'genesis_lights',pos:'center 48%',reference:'Genesis 1:14–19'},
 {word:'ABUNDANCE',scramble:'ECNADNUBA',clue:'When Genesis says the waters were to swarm with life, what is it emphasizing beyond the presence of a few fish?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD FIVE',title:'The oceans come alive',fact:'The fifth period introduces abundant aquatic life, including great sea creatures. The word swarm conveys a sea teeming with living things.',scene:'genesis_oceanlife',pos:'center 54%',reference:'Genesis 1:20–23'},
 {word:'MULTIPLY',scramble:'YLPITLUM',clue:'The blessing on creatures of the sea and sky looks beyond their creation. What were they to do over generations?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD FIVE',title:'The skies fill',fact:'Jehovah blessed aquatic and flying creatures to multiply. Genesis links the creation of life with the ability to keep producing life (Genesis 1:22).',scene:'genesis_birds',pos:'center 47%',reference:'Genesis 1:20–23'},
 {word:'VARIETY',scramble:'YTEIRAV',clue:'Genesis distinguishes domestic, wild, and other moving land animals. What feature of life does that classification highlight?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD SIX',title:'Living creatures of the land',fact:'Genesis 1:24–25 describes different kinds of land animals. The distinctions emphasize variety; they are not a modern scientific species chart.',scene:'genesis_animals',pos:'center 50%',reference:'Genesis 1:24–25'},
 {word:'PURPOSE',scramble:'ESOPRUP',clue:'Humans were not simply placed on earth to exist. What did their assignment to care for and fill the earth give their lives?',period:'CREATIVE PERIOD SIX',title:'A role for humankind',fact:'Being made in God’s image came with meaningful responsibilities: fill the earth, subdue it, and have animals in subjection. It was an assignment, not permission for cruelty.',scene:'genesis_humans',pos:'center 45%',reference:'Genesis 1:26–31'}
];

